{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads","id":864861,"title":"Where No Child of Wolf Threads","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-13T06:04:32-07:00","id":864861,"title":"Where No Child of Wolf Threads","content":"I'm pretty sure someone, somewhere has already explored the subject in a way or another, but here it goes.<br /> <br /> The Uratha and their role as spirit wardens of the passage between realms seem to be a mostly worldwide phenomena across many places, cultures &amp; societies, or directly from the writers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lodges the Splintered, pg.8</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf incorporates compatible legends of wolf-men from many different animistic cultures, european or not, as a means of broadening the setting itself,<br /> Werewolf also borrows elements from around the world and incorporates them into the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken posits a world where werewolves can be everywhere that people are found. In strange ways and odd forms, the Uratha are known around the world, even if the picture isn\u2019t always accurate. The word \u201cwerewolf\u201d becomes applicable to a great many more possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then there comes to mind a question - but what of places where little to no wolves or dogs existed?<br /> <br /> While wolves have covered a quite extensive range of places, there are also considerable regions where no wolf or dog would be found for ages until the arrival of (mostly european or near eastern) explrorers and traders. In some areas (like parts of northern africa) i guess that wild dogs, jackals - or hyenas - might or not get associated/mixed up with any Uratha sightings, but what of areas like most of Central and South America, where no convincing lookalike existed?<br /> <br /> Did no Uratha exist in those lands or where the legends about them so incredibly different due to association with other beasts or none?<br /> If no Uratha inhabited those places, why would it be so, where they untouched by the natives of Shadow, utterly overwhelmed to a degree the Uratha left little to no mark or did something else occupy the &quot;keeper of worlds&quot; niche usually filled by the Uratha in many other places?<br /> <br /> Questions, questions - so any book lore or thoughts of your own on the subject people? I would like to get some input, ideas or opinions on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:10:21-07:00","id":864868,"title":"","content":"There's no need for dogs or wolves to exist in a region for Uratha to be there. Canines provide Uratha with useful camouflage to work within, but there's no link between Forsaken werewolves and canine populations at all.<br /> <br /> In areas without dogs or wolves, Uratha have other methods of concealing their presence such as Skin Thief.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:15:31-07:00","id":864870,"title":"","content":"To be fair about South America, as per Blood of the Wolf's chapter on wolf forms in different regions, one of my character's wolf forms was much more akin to the Maned Wolf which does inhabit a large region of South American, though it is not a true wolf or even a fox, being largely unrelated to both. If Hyenas and Wild Dogs were game, I figured why not.<br /> <br /> As far as it's place in South American culture (or rather, the culture of any country therein) or myth though, I'm not really aware of any. Which may or may not be important. Might be interesting to come up with a reason for it but also probably not terribly important.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also the Coyote which I think makes it as far down as Central America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 04-13-2016, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:32:25-07:00","id":864882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864870#post864870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair about South America, as per Blood of the Wolf's chapter on wolf forms in different regions, one of my character's wolf forms was much more akin to the Maned Wolf which does inhabit a large region of South American, though it is not a true wolf or even a fox, being largely unrelated to both. If Hyenas and Wild Dogs were game, I figured why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the manned wolf is part of the reason i called out on it because, to be quite honest, it's a very flimsy association for anyone that has looked at a wolf or one of the <i>Guar\u00e1</i>. There's a reason most places outside of Brazil call it &quot;big fox&quot; or somesuch than wolf, just by looks basically, hyenas and wild dogs being game because they do make convincing predator imagery, unlike it.<br /> <br /> AFAIK, the beasts that kind of take the wolves usual mythic niches in legends of most south american legends seem to be between <i>on\u00e7as </i>(jaguars), <i>antas </i>(tapirs), <i>jacar\u00e9s </i>(caimans) and <i>queixadas </i>(peccaries), depending on locale or specific element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864870#post864870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as it's place in South American culture (or rather, the culture of any country therein) or myth though, I'm not really aware of any. Which may or may not be important. Might be interesting to come up with a reason for it.<br /> <br /> There's also the Coyote which I think makes it as far down as Central America.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, there's the Coyote - and <i>Guar\u00e1 </i>legends do have some themes in common with coyote myths, what is kind of good - but i don't know if Coyote legends relate to the Uratha in Forsaken or something else altogether, like the old Nuwisha from Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:50:00-07:00","id":864895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864882#post864882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the manned wolf is part of the reason i called out on it because, to be quite honest, it's a very flimsy association for anyone that has looked at a wolf or one of the <i>Guar\u00e1</i>. There's a reason most places outside of Brazil call it &quot;big fox&quot; or somesuch than wolf, just by looks basically, hyenas and wild dogs being game because they do make convincing predator imagery, unlike it.<br /> <br /> AFAIK, the beasts that kind of take the wolves usual mythic niches in legends of most south american legends seem to be between <i>on\u00e7as </i>(jaguars), <i>antas </i>(tapirs), <i>jacar\u00e9s </i>(caimans) and <i>queixadas </i>(peccaries), depending on locale or specific element.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> True, there's the Coyote - and <i>Guar\u00e1 </i>legends do have some themes in common with coyote myths, what is kind of good - but i don't know if Coyote legends relate to the Uratha in Forsaken or something else altogether, like the old Nuwisha from Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my brazillian stories, most Uratha use Skin Thief to resemble some large domestic dogs, or even pass as huge huskies if it is dark enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:06:55-07:00","id":864902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864895#post864895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my brazillian stories, most Uratha use Skin Thief to resemble some large domestic dogs, or even pass as huge huskies if it is dark enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually makes loads of sense for brazilian legends overall, but my interest at the moment at what distorted legends - or alternate guardians - might have filled the Uratha's niche in the South &amp; Central Americas and most of sub-saharan Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:49:07-07:00","id":864935,"title":"","content":"You aren't limited to canids, either.<br /> <br /> In first edition there was an ability similar to Skin Thief that allowed you to change into other animals, like bears or big cats. And an entire mot down there that would turn into jaguars instead of wolves, to help with their cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:34:50-07:00","id":864964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864935#post864935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't limited to canids, either.<br /> <br /> In first edition there was an ability similar to Skin Thief that allowed you to change into other animals, like bears or big cats. And an entire mot down there that would turn into jaguars instead of wolves, to help with their cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>So might Uratha in those particular part of the world have cultures tied on access to such an ability or something along those lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:42:09-07:00","id":864966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864964#post864964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So might Uratha in those particular part of the world have cultures tied on access to such an ability or something along those lines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. They're currently at war with another lodge that are descended from the Conquistadors, while both groups are dealing with the Balam-Colop, actual werejaguars that don't like werewolves.<br /> <br /> It's not uncommon at all for werewolves of certain regions to try to fit their beliefs into the evidence given to them by their new senses.<br /> <br /> But. The more they try to reject the evidence the more they're likely to find themselves butting heads with others who force their beliefs on things, or who just go with the Uratha myth. Also, it allows room for spirits and others to take advantage. If a spirit in the form of a fiery angel appears to your average Uratha, they'll appreciate that it's a spirit. For Uratha who believe they are chosen by God to hunt demons might think it's an actual divine message, giving this spirit a lot of power over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:43:55-07:00","id":864969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864966#post864966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. They're currently at war with another lodge that are descended from the Conquistadors, while both groups are dealing with the Balam-Colop, actual werejaguars that don't like werewolves.<br /> <br /> It's not uncommon at all for werewolves of certain regions to try to fit their beliefs into the evidence given to them by their new senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are those Balam-Colop described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:47:41-07:00","id":864973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864969#post864969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are those Balam-Colop described?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe the book is Blasphemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:47:49-07:00","id":864974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864969#post864969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are those Balam-Colop described?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blasphemies, p95. Right after the Brotherhood of Crossed Swords and the Lodge of Quetzal, who are at odds with one another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T09:47:35-07:00","id":865010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864974#post864974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blasphemies, p95. Right after the Brotherhood of Crossed Swords and the Lodge of Quetzal, who are at odds with one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to know, thanks a bunch you two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:38:02-07:00","id":865093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864861-where-no-child-of-wolf-threads?p=864902#post864902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually makes loads of sense for brazilian legends overall, but my interest at the moment at what distorted legends - or alternate guardians - might have filled the Uratha's niche in the South &amp; Central Americas and most of sub-saharan Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't much about other Shapeshifters in second edition <i>yet</i>. Dark Eras mentions the Bull-Shifters, and I believe we will see several others in the future. I wouldn't mind allowing players to build some custom shifters for distorted legends, if you really want to. You could do that by shifting the attribute dots received, allowing the same &quot;power gain&quot; but with other end effects. <i>Jacar\u00e9s</i> could swap that Gauru Dexterity and add it ot Stamina, for example. Other than that, I would retain all the other rules, including Auspices and Gift Acquisition. It would be a BIG FUCKING mystery to have a shifter that is another animal but has the same blessings as wolves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T01:04:18-07:00","id":865838,"title":"","content":"It's probably more interesting to have other changers in the mix, but I think humans and Uratha would both recontextualize the lupine kinship in the absence of wolves. A human society may have no conception of wolves or canines, but there's likely some large, loping predator that every sighting gets ascribed to, especially in the fever of Lunacy. <br /> The local Uratha know better, but they may see Father Wolf and the Firstborn simply as gods of the hunt. Perhaps the forms are trophies he's bestowed on his children, skins taken from wildly different beasts in the eyes of people who've never heard of wolves. Or maybe Wolf is a demon. Surely Gauru is behind some legends of ogres, oni, and giants, and perhaps even the local pack doesn't see a real distinction to force. Does it matter what creature litters that cave entrance with human bones? The Herd Must Not Know.<br /> Uratha know they aren't lions or bears, and when they roam a wilderness that has never known wolves, they know themselves to be apex predators. No wolf packs greet them as rivals or at all. Every beast is lesser, different, and mute. Nothing is kin but human, and everything is prey without constant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}